=== FOUR REAL PRODUCTION BUGS (bucket A -- the valuable part) ===

A1. THE FABRICATION GATE CORRUPTED THE ARTIFACTS IT STAMPED. (4 failures, systemic)
    adversarial_verify.py:6135-6137 stamps flagged_adversarial + corrigendum_pending onto a
    LANDED artifact -- mandated, non-destructive behaviour. But compute_artifact_checksum()
    hashed all keys except the checksum fields, so the review stamp invalidated the artifact's
    own reproducibility_checksum, and each experiment then REJECTED ITS OWN COMMITTED RECORD.
    The project's mandated review process was invalidating the very artifacts it reviewed.
    Proven by bisect on exp5610: validates at authoring commit b95dfd5a4, MISMATCHes after
    33c2e55b5 stamped it. Hit exp5610/5621/5632/5643.
    Fixed via new python/carnot/artifact_gate_annotations.py (checksum_core). Excluding ONLY
    the gate keys reproduces each stored checksum BYTE-EXACTLY -- stronger than "the mismatch
    went away": it proves the measured record was never touched and the stamp was the sole
    cause. No artifact was rewritten (never-prune). Tamper probes on honest_verdict,
    duration_s, random_seed, inference_substrate, levels_after all still caught.

A2. TWO GATE READERS DIED SILENTLY ON AN IMPORT-ALIASED CONSTANT. (9 failures, largest cluster)
    _submitted_agent_config() in experiment_4548/4560_integration_8game_gate.py AST-interprets
    module-level assignments via literal_eval. SUBMITTED_FRONTIER_TIER_COUNT = FRONTIER_TIER_COUNT
    (arc_competition_agent.py:479, itself an import alias) is not a literal, so `except: continue`
    dropped it and `constants[value_node.id]` raised a bare KeyError at the use site. ANY future
    SUBMITTED_* that becomes a Name reference killed both readers the same way.
    Fixed via new shared python/carnot/submitted_agent_config_ast.py that resolves Name->Name and
    REFUSES LOUDLY on a genuinely unresolvable name. The loud rewrite immediately exposed three
    further latent instances the KeyError had masked: GOAL_ENERGY_SOURCE (bare import),
    frozen_generator (nested dict of aliases), and a Compare/IfExp pair. Evaluator sized by
    MEASURING the config's actual AST node types, not guessing.

A5. TEST-ISOLATION LEAK IN THE VRAM GUARD FIXTURE. (0 of the 53 -- preventive; the defect named
    in the brief, confirmed)
    tests/python/test_arc_generator_vram_guard.py's fixture cleared CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_N_CTX and
    CARNOT_ARC_FFN_CPU_LAYERS but not CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU, which the conductor's
    systemd drop-in SETS -- so ambient env leaked in under xdist re-sharding and adding ANY new
    test file turned the suite red. Reproduced (margin = MINUS 258, 2 tests), fixed, and
    VALIDATED IN PRODUCTION CONDITIONS: two new test files are added in this very commit and the
    guard did not trip.
    Correct diagnosis matters here: the LOWER guard is RIGHT with FFN auto-fit on. The fixture
    was comparing an auto-fit guard against a no-offload measurement -- two different launches.
    The assertions were never wrong, they just were not told which launch to assert about. Also
    corrected the fixture docstring's false claim that it imports the module fresh.

A4. NOT FIXED, and deliberately not counted as fixed. test_jepa_curriculum_trainer.py::
    TestJEPACurriculumTrainer::test_stage3_n_pairs_includes_synthetic -- the test PASSES, the
    TEARDOWN errors on the conftest memory-leak guard (+675MB real retention). It is present in
    BOTH the before and after sets (verified by name). It briefly vanished from one sharded run;
    that was xdist flakiness, not a fix, and counting it would have been a false green.

