=== REVIEW FINDINGS APPLIED IN THIS COMMIT ===

Every finding from the adversarial review was applied. Three changed code; four corrected the
report's accounting (reflected in this message); one is argued back against with evidence.

1. A NEW NON-CAUSAL ASSERTION I INTRODUCED -- the banned "green for the wrong reason" shape.
   exp5397's default-policy assertion compared a diagnostic to the flag WITHOUT generating
   candidates first. Verified the reviewer's claim directly: the diagnostic reads False even
   with ColorBlobSaliencePrior EXPLICITLY wired, if no candidates ran. So it passed because
   nothing ran, not because the flag is off, and my comment claiming it "would have caught the
   drift" was FALSE. Now generates candidates first; verified it discriminates (default False,
   wired True) and that mutating production to ignore the flag makes it FAIL -- which it would
   not have done before. Real coverage added, not an assertion moved.

3/6. LATENT INTEGRITY BLIND SPOT IN THE NEW checksum_core (same finding, twice).
   GATE_ANNOTATION_PREFIXES matched open ("corrigendum", "flagged_adversarial"), borrowed from
   determination_preservation_lint. CONFIRMED AND WORSE THAN REPORTED: 57 distinct keys in this
   repo carry those prefixes and many are MEASURED audit tallies -- corrigendum_pending_count
   (105 occurrences), flagged_adversarial_artifacts_excluded (32), corrigendum_kinds (25),
   flagged_adversarial_count (11). Exactly the numbers an audit exists to report.
   Root cause worth naming: THE DIRECTION OF SAFETY IS INVERTED BETWEEN THE TWO USE SITES. For
   a lint catching a DROPPED determination, a broad prefix is the SAFE error. For a checksum
   exclusion deciding what NOT to hash, a broad prefix is the DANGEROUS error. The pattern was
   imported with its safety direction reversed.
   Narrowed to the three keys the gate actually writes (verified against its only write site)
   plus one bounded prefix, flagged_adversarial_cleared, for the documented *_cleared_note
   convention. Added a numeric tripwire that REFUSES to exclude an allowlisted key holding a
   number, with a bool carve-out because isinstance(True, int) is True in Python and
   flagged_adversarial is a bool. New tests/python/test_artifact_gate_annotations.py (12 tests)
   pins that flagged_adversarial_count IS hashed. Mutation-proved with 3 mutants: re-widening
   the prefix fails 2 tests, neutering the tripwire fails 1, removing the bool carve-out fails 7.
   All four real artifacts still reproduce their stored checksums byte-exactly after narrowing.

7. THE A5 FIXTURE PINNED THE NON-PRODUCTION CONFIGURATION. Correct and non-duplicative:
   clearing CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU was the right way to make the no-offload assertions
   honest, but it left the SHIPPED path (systemd sets that var, so FFN auto-fit is what runs)
   less covered than the one that does not ship. The two properties are genuinely different and
   only one was covered anywhere: ADMISSIBILITY (guard <= free) exists in
   test_arc_ffn_cpu_offload.py; SAFETY MARGIN (guard >= footprint + margin) at the auto-fit
   layer count was asserted NOWHERE -- and that is the property whose absence caused the
   original incident. Added test_the_autofit_guard_carries_real_margin_over_the_autofit_footprint
